                            "полит. жарг. член Демократической партии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "786b803b-f655-4c3c-8b48-130ec72e2745",
                        "source_entry_id": "f3d635fa-6c49-3c82-bb68-f299ef624914",
                        "target_lang_word": "democrat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "democrat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c9d69ec-3a2b-39a9-a7c3-f03c42e6f830",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee7fe0c-d888-3fe2-a8f0-a4888c405c22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supporter of democracy; an advocate of democratic politics (originally (historical) as opposed to the aristocrats in Revolutionary France)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a32230a1-34d3-4d7e-b75f-10fe9f78e633",
                                                "sense_id": "0c9d69ec-3a2b-39a9-a7c3-f03c42e6f830",
                                                "text": "The democrats now have majority control in almost all areas except the Islands District Council, where they won seven seats, and the pro-Beijing camp obtained 11 seats."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b66e15e9-2b7d-3ff1-9ead-21b01722042e",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee7fe0c-d888-3fe2-a8f0-a4888c405c22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who rules a representative democracy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3fe400a-1f3b-488f-b376-04130a6b032d",
                                                "sense_id": "b66e15e9-2b7d-3ff1-9ead-21b01722042e",
                                                "text": "Democrats have to please a large segment of the voting public and will be punished if they fail to provide public goods […] . In the case of autocrats, however, they have to please a small minority of the governing power elite […] who will punish them if they fail to dedicate the public purse to their private enrichment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61a0f8bb-c3b0-369f-a8aa-f940185d18ad",
                                        "entry_id": "6ee7fe0c-d888-3fe2-a8f0-a4888c405c22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large light uncovered wagon with two or more seats."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
